From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calvin Watford <cwatford@slack-corp.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: fix: handle unknown ObjC property attribute flag in Mantle

macOS 14.4+ / Xcode 15+ encodes optional properties with a '?' flag in
ObjC property attribute strings (e.g. "T@"NSString",?,R,C"). Mantle's
mtl_copyPropertyAttributes does not handle this flag, causing it to log
errors and — more critically — fail to decode properties used by
SQRLShipItRequest, leaving targetBundleURL nil and aborting updates.

Skip unrecognized single-character flags instead of only logging an
error, matching how 't' (old-style type encoding) is already handled.

Upstream: https://github.com/Mantle/Mantle/issues/899

diff --git a/vendor/Mantle/Mantle/extobjc/MTLEXTRuntimeExtensions.m b/vendor/Mantle/Mantle/extobjc/MTLEXTRuntimeExtensions.m
--- a/vendor/Mantle/Mantle/extobjc/MTLEXTRuntimeExtensions.m
+++ b/vendor/Mantle/Mantle/extobjc/MTLEXTRuntimeExtensions.m
@@ -666,7 +666,11 @@ mtl_propertyAttributes *mtl_copyPropertyAttributes (objc_property_t property) {

 			break;

-		default:
+		default: {
 			fprintf(stderr, "ERROR: Unrecognized attribute string flag '%c' in attribute string \"%s\" for property %s\n", flag, attrString, property_getName(property));
+			// Skip past any value associated with this flag so parsing
+			// can continue with the next attribute.
+			while (*next != ',' && *next != '\0')
+				++next;
+		}
 		}
 	}
